      "id": "cve-2026-129448",
      "kind": "exploited_flaw",
      "headline": "Apache says Roller flaw allowing pre-login code execution is under active attack",
      "summary": "Apache's CVE record says Roller 4.0.0 through 6.1.4 deserializes data at its XML-RPC endpoint before authenticating the caller, so an unauthenticated attacker can run code. The record says the flaw is being actively exploited and tells users to upgrade to 6.1.6 or later.",
      "why_it_matters": "Exploitation is confirmed by the maintainer, but Roller is a narrow product, so the reach is limited.",
